<title>BELGIUM: Luxembourg's PM says Italy in on track for EMU.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg's PM says Italy in on track for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker said on Monday that Italy was well placed to join Europe's single currency, but stressed that the Italian government needed to do more on the budgetary front.</p>
<p>&quot;The Italian convergence programme very clearly shows that Italy is moving in a good direction,&quot; Juncker told reporters ahead of a meeting of EU finance ministers here.</p>
<p>He added, however: &quot;We have to encourage them to take further steps.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom ++ 32 2 287 6830</p>
</text>
